.TH KAGI-CLUSTER-HOST 1 "September 2026" "Kagi 0.38.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-cluster-host \- distributed Kagi cluster daemon and administrative CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kagi-cluster-host
--config FILE COMMAND [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the cluster object/metadata service or issues administrative operations. The daemon integrates Raft metadata, joint-consensus membership, PQ-authenticated peer traffic, health/recovery, CLAY/MSR/Reed-Solomon erasure coding, snapshots, maintenance scheduling, capacity expansion, filesystem namespace operations, and object-backed block volumes.
.SH COMMANDS
Serve, status, object put/get, repair/scrub, health clearance, PQ identity/key operations, membership operations, snapshot operations, capacity changes, and block-volume operations are exposed through this CLI and its REST service. Use `--help` for the exact build-specific command list.
.SH CONSISTENCY
Externally visible object mutations return success only after the configured Raft commit/apply barrier. Followers do not serve stale linearizable object reads as authoritative results.
.SH SECURITY
Internal requests require configured ML-DSA identity/authentication and cluster admission credentials. Protect node private keys and persistent session/replay state.
.SH SEE ALSO
kagi-config(1), kagi-install(1), kagi-volume-nbd(1)

.SH ERASURE CODING
The runtime supports Reed-Solomon, canonical product-matrix MSR with d=2k-2, and CLAY. CLAY is the default configured EC family. With the cuda feature, data-heavy GF(256) transforms use the CUDA matrix engine when above gpu_threshold_bytes. Single-chunk CLAY/MSR recovery uses bandwidth-optimal helper requests rather than downloading complete helper chunks.
.SH TOPOLOGY MINIMUM
The daemon requires at least six configured hosts and at least six disks on every host.

.SH KAGI WEB CONSOLE
Each serving node exposes the Kagi operations console at /ui when web_console.enabled is true. The local user database stores Argon2id password hashes and viewer/admin roles. Use the web-user-add subcommand with --password-file to bootstrap users. The browser authentication exchange must be protected by TLS or a trusted TLS reverse proxy.
.PP
The console provides cluster monitoring, object/chunk locality inspection, known pending object operations, local/cluster logs, and Raft-backed bucket/WORM lifecycle administration.
